# Build output is written outside the working tree by convention. These
# patterns are a backstop for the case where a build is run without -o, not the
# primary mechanism.
/gflex
/cmd/gflex/gflex

# Go test and coverage output.
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# Nothing here ignores testdata/fuzz/, deliberately. An earlier rule did, on the
# premise that it held generated corpora -- it does not. The corpus `go test
# -fuzz` generates lives in GOCACHE and never appears in the tree; what Go
# writes to <pkg>/testdata/fuzz/<Target>/<hash> is the *minimised failing input*
# from a crash, a few bytes long, which every later plain `go test` replays as a
# subtest. That file is the regression test for the crash, so it has to be
# committable: ignoring it would mean a defect found by a fuzz run -- over the
# usbfs descriptor parser, the USB-MIDI unpacker or the frame decoders, all of
# which consume bytes from a device the threat model does not trust -- could
# never be turned into a standing test.
